; bfsodium GCM128 : AES_128 in Galois/Counter Mode  NIST SP 800_38D
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN; block/aes128table block/aes128encrypt block/copy16
; block/copy16back block/inc128 block/halve and block/ghashstep are INCLUDED;
; idiom/xor8 is PASTED  here and inside the GHASH step;
;
; IO  in:  key{16}  iv{12}  alen{2} LE  aad{alen}  plen{2} LE  pt{plen}
;     out: ciphertext{plen}  tag{16}
;
; Both lengths are read before the bytes they count  and a bfsodium primitive
; never relies on end of input; The IO is aead/chacha20poly1305's  deliberately
; so: the two AEADs in this library take the same shape of wire message;
;
; THE IV IS NINETY SIX BITS  which is the only size with a simple J0; SP
; 800_38D says that for any other length J0 is itself a GHASH  and that is a
; different program; Twelve bytes is also the only size anyone should use;
;
; THE CIPHERTEXT IS NEVER STORED; sixteen bytes are encrypted  written out and
; folded into the hash  and then the next sixteen; So the tape does not grow
; with the message  which is the rule aead/chacha20poly1305's header records
; after an earlier cut of it reached 903 thousand lines by unrolling;
;
; WHAT IS HASHED  and every piece of it padded to a whole block:
;   AAD  pad16  ciphertext  pad16  len(AAD) in bits{8}  len(C) in bits{8}
; Padding is landing a nought when the input has run out; the block being
; assembled slides a byte at a time and the slide leaves a nought behind  so
; a short block pads itself and no flag is needed;
;
; THREE CIPHER RUNS THAT ARE NOT THE KEYSTREAM; the subkey H is the cipher on
; the zero block  the tag mask is the cipher on J0  and then the counter runs
; from J0 plus one; All three put the key back first  because the schedule
; spends the window;
;
; GHASH IS THE LARGER HALF  which is worth knowing before reading the costs:
; one multiply is about three hundred million instructions against a hundred
; and fourteen million for a block of AES  so a GCM over n blocks spends most
; of its time in the field and not in the cipher;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x374  the cipher's frame  as block/aes128encrypt maps it
;   @0x375:0x384  K{16}    the key  never spent
;   @0x385:0x394  J0{16}   the pre counter block: the IV and then 0 0 0 1
;   @0x395:0x3a4  EK0{16}  the cipher on J0; the tag mask
;   @0x3a5:0x3b4  H{16}    the GHASH subkey; the cipher on the zero block
;   @0x3b5:0x3c4  the temps that keep H and J0 alive across their copies
;   @0x3c7:0x3d6  the running counter  copy16 at 967 puts it in the state
;   @0x3d7:0x3da  block/inc128's scratch
;   @0x3db:0x3ea  GB{16}  the block being assembled for the hash
;   @0x3eb:0x3fa  Y{16}   the GHASH accumulator
;   @0x400:0x4a4  block/ghashmul's frame  reached through block/ghashstep
;   @0x4b0:0x4b1  alen{2} kept  because the length block needs it after the
;                 count has been run down
;   @0x4b2:0x4b3  plen{2} kept  for the same reason
;   @0x4b4:0x4b5  remaining{2}  the working countdown
;   @0x4b6 nz  @0x4b7 more  @0x4b8 e  @0x4b9:0x4ba t u  @0x4bb j
;   @0x4bc:0x4c1  the length scratch
;   @0x4c4:0x4c7  block/halve's frame
;   @0x4cc:0x4dc  idiom/xor8 pasted at 1228

